, “What is this dream that you have dreamed? Will I and your mother and your brothers indeed come to bow ourselves down to the earth before you?” His brothers envied him, but his father kept this saying in mind.","canonicalTextHash":"1d8dc4b6e43a0f7e67121bad8ea61667b33d14d94c3ab58d200c60ad0a33f740","citation":"Genesis 37:5–11","propositionId":"engwebu:profiles02:joseph:joseph-gen-37-5-11","refId":"ref:profiles02:joseph:joseph-gen-37-5-11","referenceHash":"84dccf7d9d0598157aa9de7473c6a04d64d66a4ae249bd621625cc1ad5bf0599","sceneId":"joseph-gen-37-5-11","sourceIds":["engwebu:gen:37:5-11"],"subjectId":"joseph"}],"findings":[{"canonicalEvidence":"Joseph dreamed a dream, and he told it to his brothers, and they hated him all the more.","canonicalEvidenceHash":"4877c4dc81a7a8bc3c2c740decc8dfa2d41ef6ea5e108fa188e3be4085e33dab","citation":"Genesis 37:5–11","evidence":[{"canonicalText":"Joseph dreamed a dream, and he told it to his brothers, and they hated him all the more. He said to them, “Please hear this dream which I have dreamed: for behold, we were binding sheaves in the field, and behold, my sheaf arose and also stood upright; and behold, your sheaves came around, and bowed down to my sheaf.” His brothers asked him, “Will you indeed reign over us? Will you indeed have dominion over us?” They hated him all the more for his dreams and for his words. He dreamed yet another dream, and told it to his brothers, and said, “Behold, I have dreamed yet another dream: and behold, the sun and the moon and eleven stars bowed down to me.” He told it to his father and to his brothers. His father rebuked him, and said to him, “What is this dream that you have dreamed? Will I and your mother and your brothers indeed come to bow ourselves down to the earth before you?” His brothers envied him, but his father kept this saying in mind.","canonicalTextHash":"1d8dc4b6e43a0f7e67121bad8ea61667b33d14d94c3ab58d200c60ad0a33f740","citation":"Genesis 37:5–11","propositionId":"engwebu:profiles02:j